# This repository hashes its own files.
#
# instructions/manifest.json pins every instruction module by SHA-256 of its exact bytes, and
# src/app.mjs hashes src/*.mjs plus the app/ assets into sourceLock.runtime.files, which is bound
# into every approval request hash and checked on replay. A line ending is a byte.
#
# With core.autocrlf=true and no attributes file, git normalises to LF in the index and writes
# CRLF into the working tree on checkout. The result is a tree git reports as clean -- because it
# compares after normalising -- whose raw bytes no longer match the digests recorded against
# them. That is not a theoretical hazard: committing three instruction modules was enough to make
# every chat turn fail CHAT_CONTEXT with "Instruction module does not match its recorded digest",
# on a working tree with no uncommitted changes.
#
# So the working tree is LF on every platform. Nothing here is cosmetic.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files git must never touch, listed rather than left to detection.
*.ico binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gz binary
*.zip binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.so binary
*.dylib binary
*.sla binary
*.pdf binary
